```text
Time Limit: 1 sec
Memory: 256 MB

Description

A new cashier at a shopping counter is being trained to bill particular items. Given a list of N item prices denoted by an integer array prices, the cashier needs to only bill specific items in prices based on a given starting and ending item index.

To make this more interesting, the store manager can give the cashier multiple such starting and ending indices, denoted by Q queries. On behalf of the cashier, you need to compute the sum of item prices for each query according to these conditions.

Input Format

The first line of the input contains one integer T - the number of test cases. Then T test cases follow.

The first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers N and Q.

The second line of each test case contains N space-separated integers prices1, prices2, ..., pricesN - the price of the ith item in the list.

The next Q lines of each test case contain two space-separated integers l and r - the starting and ending index of items for each query respectively.

Output Format

For each query in a test case, print the sum of the item prices in the given interval on a new line.

Constraints

1 ≤ T ≤ 1000

1 ≤ N, Q ≤ 10^5

-10^9 ≤ prices[i] ≤ 10^9

1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ N

It is guaranteed that the sum of N and Q over all test cases is ≤ 10^6.

Sample Input 1

1
5 1
10 20 30 40 50
1 3

Sample Output 1

60

Sample Input 2

1
5 2
1 1 1 1 1
1 3
2 5

Sample Output 2

3
4

Note

In Sample Input 1,

The given array = 10, 20, 30, 40, 50.

For the only query, l = 1 and r = 3, so ans = 10 + 20 + 30 = 60.

In Sample Input 2,

The given array = 1, 1, 1, 1, 1.

For the first query, l = 1 and r = 3, so ans = 1 × 3 = 3.

For the second query, l = 2 and r = 5, so ans = 1 × 4 = 4.
```



#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl

void solve() {
    int n,q;
    cin>>n>>q;

    vector<ll>v(n+1);
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        cin>>v[i];
    }
    vector<ll>prefix(n+1);
    prefix[0] = v[0];
    for(int i = 1; i < n; i++)
    {
        prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] + v[i];
    }

    while(q--)
    {
        int l,r;
        cin>>l>>r;
        l--;
        r--;
        if(l == 0)
        {
            cout<<prefix[r]<<endl;
        }
        else
        {
            cout<<(prefix[r] - prefix[l-1])<<endl;
        }
    }

}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}
